---
import DocsLayout from '../../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quick Start — MHA Manager"
  description="Run your first MHA Manager job in five steps."
  currentSlug="quick-start"
>

  <div class="doc-header">
    <h1 class="doc-title">Quick Start</h1>
    <p class="doc-lead">
      The fastest path to results — a single Mono job from open panel to exported AnimSequence.
      Assumes the plugin is already installed and the required engine plugins are enabled.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="callout callout-tip">
    <strong>New to MetaHuman Animator?</strong> You'll need a <code>UFootageCaptureData</code> asset
    and a <code>UMetaHumanIdentity</code> asset already set up in your project before continuing.
    These are created through the standard MetaHuman Animator workflow in the editor.
  </div>

  <div class="steps">

    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">1</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3 class="step-title">Open the MHA Manager panel</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          From the menu bar, go to <strong>Window → MHA Manager</strong>.
          The panel will dock into the editor. You can float or re-dock it anywhere.
        </p>
        <figure class="doc-figure">
          <div class="doc-img-placeholder">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="placeholder-icon"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><line x1="20" y1="4" x2="20" y2="4.01"/></svg>
            <span class="placeholder-name">qs-panel-empty.webp</span>
            <span class="placeholder-hint">The MHA Manager tab open and docked — empty queue, Global Settings panel visible at top</span>
          </div>
          <figcaption>The MHA Manager panel on first open — empty queue with Global Settings at the top</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">2</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3 class="step-title">Set your output path</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          In the <strong>Global Settings</strong> panel at the top, set <strong>Output Path</strong>
          to a Content Browser folder where generated assets should land — for example
          <code>/Game/Captures/Processed</code>. The default is <code>/Game/MHA_Batch</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">3</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3 class="step-title">Add a Mono job</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          Click <strong>Add Job</strong>. A new row appears in the queue. Set the job type
          to <strong>Mono</strong>, then assign your assets in the row's cells:
        </p>
        <div class="asset-table">
          <div class="asset-row header">
            <span>Column</span>
            <span>What to assign</span>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-row">
            <span><strong>Capture Data</strong></span>
            <span>Your <code>UFootageCaptureData</code> asset</span>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-row">
            <span><strong>Identity</strong></span>
            <span>Your <code>UMetaHumanIdentity</code> asset</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="step-desc" style="margin-top:12px;">
          If both assets are under a predictable folder structure, the plugin may auto-discover
          the Identity — check the cell before assigning manually.
        </p>
        <figure class="doc-figure">
          <div class="doc-img-placeholder">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="placeholder-icon"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><line x1="20" y1="4" x2="20" y2="4.01"/></svg>
            <span class="placeholder-name">qs-job-configured.webp</span>
            <span class="placeholder-hint">Queue showing one Mono job row with Capture Data and Identity cells filled in</span>
          </div>
          <figcaption>A configured Mono job — Capture Data and Identity assigned, job type set to Mono</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">4</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3 class="step-title">Start the batch</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          Click <strong>Start Batch</strong>. The plugin will validate the job, then run it
          through the full pipeline:
        </p>
        <div class="pipeline-steps">
          <span class="pipeline-step">Validate Input</span>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <span class="pipeline-step">Process Performance</span>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <span class="pipeline-step">Export Outputs</span>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <span class="pipeline-step">Save Assets</span>
        </div>
        <p class="step-desc" style="margin-top:12px;">
          Progress is shown per-job in the queue row. The log panel below the queue streams
          live output from the solver.
        </p>
        <figure class="doc-figure">
          <div class="doc-img-placeholder">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="placeholder-icon"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><line x1="20" y1="4" x2="20" y2="4.01"/></svg>
            <span class="placeholder-name">qs-batch-running.webp</span>
            <span class="placeholder-hint">Panel mid-process — job row showing progress bar and current stage label, log panel scrolling below</span>
          </div>
          <figcaption>The batch running — per-job progress bar and live log output visible</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="step-num">5</div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <h3 class="step-title">Find your outputs</h3>
        <p class="step-desc">
          When the job completes, your generated assets appear in the output path you set in step 2:
        </p>
        <div class="asset-table">
          <div class="asset-row header">
            <span>Asset type</span>
            <span>Description</span>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-row">
            <span><code>UMetaHumanPerformance</code></span>
            <span>The solved performance — re-processable any time</span>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-row">
            <span><code>AnimSequence</code></span>
            <span>Baked facial animation on the MetaHuman skeleton</span>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-row">
            <span><code>LevelSequence</code></span>
            <span>Sequencer-ready animation track (if enabled in Global Settings)</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="doc-figure">
          <div class="doc-img-placeholder">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="placeholder-icon"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><line x1="20" y1="4" x2="20" y2="4.01"/></svg>
            <span class="placeholder-name">qs-content-browser-output.webp</span>
            <span class="placeholder-hint">Content Browser showing the output folder — Performance asset, AnimSequence, and LevelSequence visible</span>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Generated assets in the Content Browser after a successful batch</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div class="callout callout-note" style="margin-top:32px;">
    <strong>Processing multiple takes?</strong> Add more jobs before clicking Start Batch —
    you don't need to run them one at a time. The queue processes them sequentially and saves
    a manifest automatically at <code>Saved/MHAManager/batch.mhajson</code> when done.
  </div>

  <div class="doc-footer">
    <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/installation" class="prev-link">
      <span class="nav-label">Previous</span>
      <span class="nav-title">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M19 12H5M12 5l-7 7 7 7"/></svg>
        Installation
      </span>
    </a>
    <a href="/marketplace/mha-manager/docs/job-types" class="next-link">
      <span class="nav-label">Next</span>
      <span class="nav-title">
        Job Types
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  /* Image placeholders */
  .doc-figure { margin: 20px 0 4px; }
  .doc-img-placeholder {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 80%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 36px 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .placeholder-icon { color: var(--text-muted); opacity: 0.35; }
  .placeholder-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.775rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .placeholder-hint { font-size: 0.775rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 480px; line-height: 1.5; }
  figcaption { font-size: 0.775rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-align: center; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }

  .doc-header { margin-bottom: 32px; }

  .doc-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .doc-lead {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 580px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .callout {
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    border-left: 3px solid;
  }

  .callout-tip {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, transparent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .callout-note {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, #f0a500 8%, transparent);
    border-color: #f0a500;
  }

  .callout strong { font-weight: 600; }

  .callout code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .step:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .step-num {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--accent);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .step-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .step-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .step-desc strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .step-desc code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .asset-table {
    margin-top: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .asset-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.6fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .asset-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .asset-row.header {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .asset-row strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }

  .asset-row code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.775rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .pipeline-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }

  .pipeline-step {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 5px 12px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .pipeline-arrow {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .doc-footer {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 28px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .prev-link, .next-link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
    min-width: 140px;
  }

  .prev-link { align-items: flex-start; }
  .next-link { align-items: flex-end; }
  .prev-link:hover, .next-link:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }

  .nav-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .nav-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .step { flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  }
</style>
